Article 22
In order to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, parents and family:
a. protect women and children from various violations of rights within the household;
b. encourage the formation of a harmonious, educative and democratic family;
c. provide good example to children in accordance with religious and customary teachings;
d. supervise children in their activities inside or outside the home; and e. provide opportunities for children to dialogue and express opinions democratically.

Article 64
(1) The policy for the development of KLA is directed towards the fulfillment of Children's rights which are divided into 5 (five) groups, comprising:
a. civil rights and freedoms;
b. family environment and alternative care;
c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, utilization of leisure time, and cultural activities; and e. Special protection.
(2) Further provisions regarding the policy for the development of KLA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 9
The Regional Gender Mainstreaming Working Group as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter c has the following tasks:
a. promoting and facilitating Gender Mainstreaming to each OPD;
b. conducting socialization and advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to Sub-district Heads and Wali Nagari;
c. preparing work programs every year;
d. encouraging the realization of Gender Responsive planning and budgeting;
e. preparing the work plan of the Gender Mainstreaming working group every year;
f. being responsible to the Regent through the Vice Regent;
g. formulating gender mainstreaming policy recommendations to the Regent;
h. preparing the Regional Gender profile;
i. monitoring the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in each OPD;
j. establishing a technical team to conduct analysis of the Regional budget;
k. preparing a regional action plan on Gender Mainstreaming in the Region; and
l. encouraging the implementation of selection and appointment of focal points in each OPD.

Article 20
(1) In order to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government:
a. conducts socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women and children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. provides guidelines on handling acts of violence against women and children;
c. involves community participation in recovery and reintegration; d. develops an integrated database and information system regarding acts of violence against women and children;
e. develops family empowerment programs;
f. strengthens the function of community organizations working in the field of women's empowerment and child protection; and
g. provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women and children.
(2) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by OPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual;
g. informatics and communication; and
h. peace and order.
(3) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by OPD in accordance with their respective fields of duty in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

